{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>ארפא</b> — The word משובה is pejorative throughout Scripture, and it is not like saying משובתם in every place where I struck them, but rather the turning of the soul, like illness in the body; therefore the word ארפא corresponds to 'I struck Ephraim.'" "<b>אהבם</b> — Love of willingness, the opposite of 'Elohai, I rejected them.'" "<b>כי שב</b> — The opposite of 'My anger burned against them.'"], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:14.024277367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}